1. Data is stored as `exportname/TREEXXXX/.../FILEXXXX` — a tree of files.
2. Files and directories are auto-created.
3. Files are deleted when the corresponding block is marked unused (TRIM → delete_treefile).
4. Individual block files are fixed 4096 bytes (TREEPAGESIZE).
5. At most 1024 files/subdirectories per folder (TREEDIRSIZE).
6. Nesting depth is chosen so the whole tree covers `filesize` bytes.
7. filesize must be specified (required).
8. Mutually exclusive with multifile; treefiles takes precedence.

